# Rover 6 hp two-seater, 1905-1912.
#
# The single-cylinder Rover: a light open two-seater with a 780/812 cc engine,
# the model that sat below the Rover 8 and sold in almost the same numbers.
# About 2,296 built.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rover_6
#
# Dimensions 2.819 x 1.219 x about 1.40 m (height estimated), wheelbase 1.829 m.
#
# Shape reference: no broadside photograph of a Rover 6 exists in the pack; the
# side slot is a front three-quarter about 45 degrees off, both wheels visible.
# The flank and tail are estimated from that view and the published dimensions.
# The limitation is recorded. Two Commons files titled as 6 hp cars were
# rejected as 1329 cc cars of a different model.
#
# Colours: grade (d), no period UK document consulted. Black, Green, Maroon and
# Grey are plain colour names, the common finishes of the period. Weights 2, 2,
# 1, 1, total 6, provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 45 km/h. Comfort 18/357, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 18. Classes 2,3.
# Dates 1905-1912 production, road tail staggered 1922-1924.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/rover-6.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/rover-6.dae. References: citycars/references/rover-6/
# (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: no broadside photograph exists; the side slot is a front
# three-quarter about 45 degrees off, with an elevated rear three-quarter and a
# front detail. The flank and tail are estimates. The open, windscreen-free car
# is modelled and has no glazing; the windscreen-and-hood variant is not
# represented. Two Commons files titled as 6 hp cars were rejected as 1329 cc
# cars of a different model.


obj=citycar
name=Rover6(Black)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=2
intro_year=1905
intro_month=1
retire_year=1924
retire_month=6
speed=45
class=2,3
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=18
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=357

